 ## Measured semantics — out of scope
 
-These two properties of `src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.ts` are recorded so the hook features that follow specify against real behaviour. This issue changes none of them; each is a separate, out-of-scope change owned by no issue in this epic.
+These properties of `src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.ts` record the measured semantics that hook features specify against. The `onError` boundary remains out of scope.
 
 - The `catch` gates `onError` on `error instanceof Error` ([chatOrchestrator.ts#L150](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.ts#L150)), so a rejection that is not an `Error` — a thrown string or object — bypasses `onError` entirely while still propagating to the caller.
-- `afterModelResponse` is called once per user message after the round loop exits ([chatOrchestrator.ts#L148](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.ts#L148)), and is passed the `lastUsage` local — the most recent round's usage, not a sum across tool rounds, so a deployer using the hook for billing or audit under-counts every turn that ran tools.
+- `afterModelResponse` is called once per user message after the round loop exits and receives the summed provider-call usage for the entire turn, so tool rounds are included in a deployer's billing or audit total ([validated by: reports the summed usage from every provider call in a turn with two tool rounds](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestratorUsage.acceptance.test.ts#L44) and [validated by: accumulates usage across multiple tool rounds](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.test.ts#L555)).
+- When one or more rounds report usage, the total is the sum of the reported fields; when none report usage, the hook receives `undefined` ([validated by: counts reported rounds while leaving a turn with no reported usage undefined](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestratorUsage.acceptance.test.ts#L67)).
+- If an earlier round reports usage and a later round does not, the usage reported to `afterModelResponse` is the usage from the earlier round ([validated by: keeps the usage an earlier round reported when a later round reports none](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.test.ts#L544)).
+- Summing two usage records adds each token field ([validated by: sums token counts from two usage records](../../src/orchestration/usageAccumulator.test.ts#L5)).
+- When the accumulated usage is `undefined`, the sum is the next value ([validated by: returns next when accumulated is undefined](../../src/orchestration/usageAccumulator.test.ts#L14)).
+- When the next usage is `undefined`, the sum is the accumulated value ([validated by: returns accumulated when next is undefined](../../src/orchestration/usageAccumulator.test.ts#L22)).
+- When both usage values are `undefined`, the sum is `undefined` ([validated by: returns undefined when both are undefined](../../src/orchestration/usageAccumulator.test.ts#L30)).
